    ],
    "built": 1527,
    "note": "Nasrid works of the 13th–14th centuries with no recorded architects (the Alcazaba begun by Muhammad I c. 1238, the palaces of Comares and of the Lions under Yusuf I, d. 1354, and Muhammad V, d. 1391; the Generalife c. 1300–1319, its upper storey 1494). The Palace of Charles V was designed by Pedro Machuca in 1527 and continued by his son Luis; its roof was finished in 1967 to the old design. 'built' = the design of the Palace of Charles V, the latest major work. Every author died centuries ago."
  },
