  "notes": "Built by code (model_sources/Q47476_alhambra.py, tools/meshkit.py) with AI assistance. The whole walled city on the Sabika hill and the Generalife across the ravine, on the real terrain (ground: keep): the 2.2 km of walls in reddish rammed earth following the ground (walk 9.5 m above the outside ground or 3 m above the inside, parapet and Nasrid merlons), 35 towers and gates from OpenStreetMap, the Alcazaba with the Torre de la Vela and its bell gable and the foundations of the Plaza de Armas, the Nasrid Palaces at one floor level (y = −3) with the Comares tower, the Court of the Myrtles with its pool, hedges and porticoes, the Court of the Lions with 124 columns, its two pavilions, the fountain with twelve lions and the four channels, the halls with tiled hipped roofs (the roofs of irregular plans are generated from the distance to the eaves), the Palace of Charles V (two orders, round windows, marble portals on the west and south, the circular courtyard with 32 + 32 columns, the 1967 tiled roof), the Partal with the Torre de las Damas and its pool, the medina (Calle Real houses, Santa María, the Parador, ruins as low walls), and the Generalife palace around the Patio de la Acequia (channel with jets, beds, porticoes, the gallery of 18 arches, the Sala Regia and the mirador tower, the Patio de la Sultana) with its gardens and cypress rows. Heights of most halls and towers are estimated from photos (±15–20 %); the Comares tower is 25 m above the court of the Myrtles (44 m above the bottom of its foundations, 45 m from its real foot), the Torre de la Vela 20 m and the Torre del Homenaje 18 m above the Plaza de Armas. Trees inside gardens are placed at random (the real ones are not mapped one by one). Not modelled: the terrain, the streets, the woods outside the walls, the interiors and the stucco, the buildings outside the walls. The footprint covers the walls (+6 m) and the Generalife (+3 m) joined.",
